From: pletch <17855860+pletch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:54:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dummynet_st: the AQMs' clock from uptime, not ticks

The fourth of the sub-tick release series (opnsense-cake SUBTICK.md).
CoDel, PIE, FQ-CoDel and FQ-PIE stamp packets and measure their sojourn
with AQM_UNOW, which was curr_time * tick: the delay in steps of a tick,
1 ms at kern.hz=1000 and 10 ms at 100, against a 5 ms target. With
releases between ticks the packets leave much sooner than that, so the
AQMs now read the uptime in us (sbinuptime()), as CAKE does; it is
truncated to aqm_time_t and wraps as before. The unused NOW (ms) stays.
---
 sys/netpfil/ipfw/dn_aqm.h | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/dn_aqm.h b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/dn_aqm.h
index 50a6ed7799a..50ea245c872 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/dn_aqm.h
+++ b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/dn_aqm.h
@@ -39,7 +39,13 @@
 /* NOW is the current time in millisecond*/
 #define NOW ((V_dn_cfg.curr_time * tick) / 1000)
 
-#define AQM_UNOW (V_dn_cfg.curr_time * tick)
+/*
+ * The AQMs' clock, us (SUBTICK.md): uptime, not dummynet's ticks, so that
+ * CoDel, PIE, FQ-CoDel and FQ-PIE see a packet's sojourn as it is rather
+ * than in steps of a tick. Truncated to aqm_time_t, which wraps as the
+ * tick-based value did.
+ */
+#define AQM_UNOW ((aqm_time_t)sbttous(sbinuptime()))
 #define AQM_TIME_1US ((aqm_time_t)(1))
 #define AQM_TIME_1MS ((aqm_time_t)(1000))
 #define AQM_TIME_1S ((aqm_time_t)(AQM_TIME_1MS * 1000))
